1) Base case ko bhar do

code: class Solution {
    public int fib(int n) {
        int[] dp = new int[n+1];

        //pehle base ko bhar do
        dp[0] = 0;
        dp[1] = 1;

        //ab baki values ko dekh ke bharo 
        // baki values ko bharne ke liye usi formula ko dekho
        //dp[n] = fib(n-1)+fib(n-2);
        //dp[i] = fib(i-1)+fib(i-2);

        for(int i=2;i<=n;i++)
        {
            dp[i]=dp[i-1]+dp[i-2];
        }
        return dp[n];
    }
}

TC: O(N)
SC: O(N)  (for dp array)

Space Optimization: ab hume sirf 2 hi values ki jarurat hai nth value nikalne ke liye toh kyu itna bada array banaye 

code: class Solution {
    public int fib(int n) {
        if(n<=1) return n;
        if(n==2) return 1;
        int[] dp = new int[3];
        dp[0] = 0;
        dp[1] = 1;
        dp[2] = 1;
        for(int i=3;i<=n;i++)
        {
            dp[0] = dp[1];
            dp[1] = dp[2];
            dp[2] = dp[0]+dp[1];
        }
        return dp[2];
    }
}

T.C. -> O(N)
SC.  -> O(1) 

